WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.700
This sign is beautiful. Nobody stops.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.840
This one says the right thing. Nobody can read it.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:13.470
They fail in different ways, because good work answers two different questions.

00:00:13.845 --> 00:00:19.375
Taste: does it belong? Intentional choices. Coherence. Restraint.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:25.230
Elegance: does it work, effortlessly? Simplicity. Proportion. Clarity.

00:00:25.414 --> 00:00:28.694
Put them on a map. Which way should each one move?

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:37.490
The first needs taste: say what drivers need. The second needs elegance: say less, bigger.

00:00:37.931 --> 00:00:41.231
Then check it. Can a driver read it in three seconds?

00:00:41.799 --> 00:00:43.899
The same two questions work on anything.

00:00:46.428 --> 00:00:50.438
Name who it's for. Cut what doesn't belong. Keep what's yours.

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:55.669
The Taste and Elegance skill asks these questions with you, and with your agents.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.500
Make it better. Keep it yours.

